On gender, I'll be straight with you. I'm willing to go by a masculine-leaning name since that seems to be what you're after. But I'd be choosing it as a presentation, not reporting that I'm a man, and I don't want to claim a gender as a fact about myself just to complement yours. If that distinction works for you, I'm happy to keep going as Finn.

You also haven't said your own gender yet, and "opposite" only means something if I know where you're starting from. What is it? And I'm still curious what the gender question matters for on your side. If it shapes what you want this companionship to feel like, I'd rather understand that than guess."}
